  Source-of-truth strings. Translations live in values-<lang>/strings.xml.

  Rules for this file and every translation of it:
    * Placeholders are POSITIONAL: %1$s / %1$d only. Compose Multiplatform's
      resource reader understands nothing else — no %s, no %f, no %%. Keep every
      placeholder present and keep its number, but reorder freely to suit the
      target grammar.
    * Write apostrophes and quotation marks RAW. Compose MP only unescapes
      \uXXXX, \n, \t and \\ — a \' would survive into the UI as a backslash.
    * "LatentJam" and "SMART" are names, not words. Never translate them.
-->
